Z||000000||Greg Piet||08-15-2001||08:34 PM||||I never renewed my FOCOA membership because I really didnt get anything out of it, except a few magazines that I got about 2 months past the month on the mag.  <P>Now I just got one with a big PAST DUE stamp on it!<P>I never asked to get renewed so I am tempted to tell FOCOA to stick it in their ear which I know isnt nice, but if I dont renew my subscription to Car and Driver, or the Sports Car club of America, or the American Physical Society, it just ends and I am no longer a member and not getting their publications.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 SM<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">    <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||08-15-2001||08:58 PM||||The last mag I got from them had "the stamp" on it too.  My membership was actually up last January.<P>I do like to get their rag, even though it isn't the best edited thing in the world.  I find they usually have some interesting stuff in there.  I just have a problem giving them over $30 a year for 4 rags that get shrunk into two or three a year with a "combined issue" to make it all right.  I spend less on Motor Trend and Car and Driver together!  They always give me the correct number of mags and usually have gramatically correct sentances and correctly spelled words.  No only if they'd cover Fiero's every issue  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||08-15-2001||09:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Greg Piet:<BR><B>I never renewed my FOCOA membership because I really didnt get anything out of it, except a few magazines <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I hope you can at least enjoy this  edition because my car is there twice!!!!<P>Once for the Daytona show & once for the Carlisle show !!<P>You might not notice the Daytona shot, as for the babe's in the next picture !<P>(they got my name wrong in the 2nd pic)||||reg||6
Z||000003||Formula88||08-15-2001||11:59 PM||||Well, automatic renewals have to be disclosed in advance.  Otherwise, consider anyting else they send you a gift.  That's according to the USPS and Federal Law.  If you receive something in the mail you didn't ask for, you are not obligated to pay for or return it.||||reg||6
